        "id": 1177449
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-18T03:50:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry for the confusion caused by the term \"hardcoded.\"\nWhat I actually meant is that the RO size is defined via DTS, not hardcoded in the driver.\n\n```\n#define CONFIG_WP_STORAGE_SIZE CONFIG_EC_PROTECTED_STORAGE_SIZE\n#define CONFIG_EC_PROTECTED_STORAGE_SIZE DT_PROP(_BINMAN_RO_PATH, size)\n```\nSo the protection range is determined by configuration (DTS) with different projects, rather than being fixed in the code.\n\n\u003eCan the cros_flash driver set different protection ranges using the same library and rom code?\n\nYes, we expect the cros_flash driver to support different RO sizes (e.g., CONFIG_WP_STORAGE_SIZE) while using the same library and ROM code.\n\nThat is why the API is designed to take parameters (e.g., uint32_t offset, size_t page_count) instead of relying on fixed values in library.",
      "parentUuid": "115b6205_50d0bfca",
      "revId": "c768fb84b0673458119d52d90e855e2d801ac088",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
